# Xpress baseline controls (FlexTool default).
#
# Format: one "<CONTROL> <value>" per line; "#" starts a comment.
# FlexTool turns each line into ``setControl <CONTROL> <value>`` and pipes it
# to the ``optimizer`` console before ``readprob <mps>`` / ``lpoptimize``
# (flextool/engine/solve/_subprocess_solve.py).  Xpress' own ``.ctl`` /
# ``readcontrols`` is not used: it differs between Xpress versions.
#
# FlexTool's Xpress driver solves linear problems only: a solve with integer
# variables stops with a message.  MAXTIME is whole seconds.
#
# Precedence (later wins): this file < the solve's solver_mip_gap < the solve's
# solver_arguments < the run's --solver-mip-gap / --solver-time-limit (or
# FLEXTOOL_SOLVER_MIP_GAP / FLEXTOOL_SOLVER_TIME_LIMIT; the GUI's time limit).
# Names match without regard to case; one value per parameter is passed.
#
# FlexTool reads this file from the run's solver_config folder (see
# docs/solvers/index.md, "Where the option files come from") and copies it to
# <work folder>/solve_data/solver_config/ as the record of the run.
#
# Reference: https://www.fico.com/fico-xpress-optimization/docs/dms2024-01/solver/optimizer/HTML/chapter6.html
#
# Conservative defaults — edit to suit your model.
# Replaced by the run's --threads (Threads per run in the FlexTool window) when it is given.
THREADS 1
MIPRELSTOP 0.002
OUTPUTLOG 1
